Now this prompt was just silly, my PC Blade Dancer
was wearing hard shoes at the time, and standing on
the Mines Town altar about to try on the watch
captain's garb:

    Take off what? [boOT or ?*]

FWIW

xanthian.

   The Rest of the Story, but not by Paul Harvey

I managed to heal my large cat Cat Dancing three
times during her battle, which let her survive
taking down the watch captain, so now I have a
silver saber for my troubles and my cat has some
pittance of HPs left. I got my nine points of
protection AC improvement, barely afforded, having
done Sokoban before Mines because I found some +2
elven mithral dropped by an unlucky hobbit in the
main dungeon, and didn't _need_ any other wonderful
armor from Mines quite so early.

My armor class tricked out in everything but a shirt
is now AC:-15, not much is enchanted, four total
points of armor enchantment is all.

The game is rife with shops, with general stores on
levels 2, 3, and 4 so far, though I had to find a
key before I could open the shop door on DLVL 2, so
accumulating zorkmids was fairly easy.  My over
10,500z just did suffice to bribe the priest of
Posidon for 9 AC worth of protection, without
bothering to bankrupt any Mines Town shops yet,
because I ran over some monsters by typing too fast
and arrived at XL:3.

I also found a hearsed bones top mines level of
Valkerie Maniac and Dognap the kitten; anyone want
to claim them? What kind of a Valk shows up in Mines
1 with 79z to her name? Do Valks take vows of
poverty? This one looked like a speed ascension
attempt gone terribly wrong on someone's part. I
think the killer bees may have done for her. I was
lucky my wand of sleep still had some charges to let
the pets take care of them.

The most satisfying thing so far in this game is
that I just invented for myself a new way to solve
the "oR version of toplevel Sokoban that is _so_
much easier that the way I had been using, there's
no way I'll ever go back. Also, there was a (BoH in
one of the shops, so Sokoban was the correct flavor
to give me the better choice prize, I have
reflection (and two other uncursed but UnIDed
amulets) and so I know I want specifically [GDSM if
I find a wish.

I have a puppy, a kitten, and a dog along for the
ride, acquired after solving Sokoban.

Cat Dancing, with her 72HPs by top level Sokoban,
since I got to top level Sokoban (at DLVL 2) before
I ran into some monsters that pushed me to XL:2, had
only the easiest monsters to fight, so she went
through the treasure zoo like a tasmanian devil in
heat or maybe food deprived for a week. When I could
get in the door, there was nothing in sight but
stacks of gold, a few dropped objects, and one
lonely zombie hiding in a far corner. Later I found
a sewer rat in one closet, though.

I've also converted an altar on DLVL 1.

Collectively, this game is providing the kind of
good luck that would let any skilled player win the
game handily. I'm going to see if I can at least
survive the trip to Mines End next, I think.

So far I haven't found a scroll of ID, my biggest
deficit to date.  I have two +1 rings of protection,
a ring of levitation, and a ring of invisibility, a
wand of lightning, a wand of magic missile, two
wands of sleep, and some unIDed wands.  Boudewijn is
still correct, this game is all about IDing stuff,
and I'm way behind the power curve in that regard.

One strategy improvement in this game was
deliberately to pray for food every other time my PC
got weak. This resulted in leaving Sokoban with
quite a bit of surplus food, where usually, the PC
eats all that is found and then starves there
instead.

Is saber skill the same as long sword skill, so that
I can hope to become unrestricted with a healer?

I have a leash and know where some magic traps are.
Is there anything useful to do urging pets to walk
on magic traps, or are polymorph traps the only good
ones?

While I'm asking questions, is it possible to drag a
pile of gold out of a shop with an iron hook? If so,
how?



